# ROADMAP: human-readable CSR restore table (per engine)

Goal: every engine registration ships a human-readable `csr_restore_table.md`
answering, per CSR: can this engine restore it and which condition is met --
or why not / which condition is unmet.

## Scope decision 2026-07-06 (user)

NO spec/PDF work. The original plan ordered the table by the per-core
datasheet (DS220 Ch.22 tables) and required PDF mining (old F1). The user
descoped that: the report is built ONLY from the existing
`csr_manifest.csv` (manifest order = spec-inventory order). DS220-based
ordering and the DS-as-authority skill rewrite are dropped, not deferred.

## Features

- [x] **F2' renderer + reason dict.** `tests/engines/render_restore_table.py`
  (stdlib only): `csr_manifest.csv` -> `<engine>/csr_restore_table.md`, three
  groups (restored / implemented-not-restored / not-implemented), plain-English
  reason dictionary for the EXCL_*/CONST_RO/NEW dispositions, markdown-safe
  cell escaping. Unit test: `tests/engines/test_restore_table.py`
  (inline fixtures, 15 checks). Done 2026-07-06.

- [x] **F3' wire + regenerate + guard.** Generated for both registered engines
  (`ax45mpv_premium-5bea8bdc`, `ax46mpv_advanced-a13f86a3`). Drift guard
  `tests/engines/test_restore_table.sh` = unit test + regenerate + diff
  (hand-edit or stale table FAILS; verified both directions). Contract updated:
  `tests/engines/README.md` artifact list, `docs/USER_GUIDE.md` pointer,
  skill `references/engine-registration.md` dir sketch. Done 2026-07-06.

- [x] **F6 dedupe gen_manifest.py.** ONE shared generator
  `tests/engines/gen_manifest.py` (generic recursive wire resolver handles
  both decoder generations); per-engine dirs keep only data
  (`rtl_params.json`: params + the rare generate-block wire override).
  Byte-parity proven against golden captures of both old generators AND the
  committed manifests. Per-engine copies deleted. Done 2026-07-06.

- [x] **F7 probe by default ("measure, don't model").** gen_manifest.py now
  AUTO-RUNS `probe_engine.sh` -- the measured probe is the only source for
  `implemented` + `reset_value`; `ANDESIM_PROBE_CSV` merely reuses a capture;
  the RTL-equation fallback is legal ONLY for `EXCL_SIDEFX` probe skips
  (anything else missing fails loudly). Gate:
  `tests/engines/test_gen_manifest_probe.sh` (probe-sourced manifest ==
  committed; missing non-SIDEFX CSR fails). The dead baseline-capture parsing
  was removed. Done 2026-07-06.

